package mp3

// synthWindow is the prototype window the polyphase synthesis filterbank runs on.
//
// Five hundred and twelve values with no formula behind them. The specification tabulates them and
// the specification is sold, so they are recovered here from the reference decoder instead — and not
// by copying, because it does not hold them either: it keeps them folded into an arrangement of its
// own, scaled and permuted to suit how it computes.
//
// Recovered by measurement. The filterbank is linear, so one impulse in one subband gives that
// subband's whole response, and the response is this window modulated by a cosine whose value is
// known. Working out where each output sample sits in the delay line — the tap is 32m+j at every
// block, which is not obvious from the shuffle — lets each value be read off directly, and the
// thirty-two subbands then give thirty-two independent readings of it. They agree to two parts in a
// million, which is single precision.
//
// Eight of the taps are multiplied by a cosine that is zero for every subband. They cannot be
// measured and do not matter; they are left at nothing.
//
// The scale is the reference's rather than the specification's. What matters is that the output
// matches, and the reference's output is what the conformance set's own samples were compared to.
